message: "If you use these certificates or verifiers, please cite this release."
title: "MathIS Sidon Frontier: R9, R16 and Exact Two-Sided Certificates"
authors:
  - family-names: "Williams"
    given-names: "Ariel M."
version: "1.3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23555594"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/FromAriel/mathis-sidon-frontier"
abstract: >-
  Exact rational R9, R16, seven historical asymmetric two-sided Sidon smoothing
  certificates and one stronger recovered certificate, with standalone
  standard-library Python verifiers. The strongest included certificate proves
  sqrt(ab) < 0.942809270635 using Akwei's ramp construction within the Hou-Zhao
  lineage. Its exact declared bound is below the fixed reported Akwei bound
  0.942809522 and the cited Wu/wustep q2 coefficient. No current record,
  novelty, optimality, exponent advance or solution of Erdos Problem 30 is
  claimed. Development and review used AI-assisted workflows.
keywords:
  - Sidon sets
  - additive combinatorics
  - exact rational certificate
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Mathematical Integrity System
license: MIT
